family: set-cli
what: poll
transport: v3
address: 192.0.2.10
verification: reference
reference: common set-style SNMP statements (set snmp community …, set snmp v3 …); RFC 3414 (USM) and RFC 3415 (VACM)
does: Lets Woodshed poll the device's SNMP agent (SNMPv3, read-only).
check: Devices → Add polling → Test poll answers with the device's name and interfaces; after the first cycle the device page shows its graphs.
placeholders: <V3-USER> <AUTH-PASSPHRASE> <PRIV-PASSPHRASE>
addresses: 192.0.2.10 2001:db8::10 logs-01.example.net logs-01
notes:
- Reference only: not tested on a device; check your device's documentation.
- The statements follow the SNMPv3 access model (RFC 3415): the user joins a group, and the group may read a view. The keywords for each piece differ between devices.
- Add the same user in Woodshed: Settings → SNMP → v3 users, name <V3-USER>, SHA-256 and AES-128, with the same passphrases.
- Then add the device in Woodshed: Devices → Add polling, its address, SNMPv3 and the user <V3-USER>.
---- part cli "": Enter in configuration mode, then commit
set snmp v3 usm local-engine user <V3-USER> authentication-sha256 authentication-password <AUTH-PASSPHRASE>
set snmp v3 usm local-engine user <V3-USER> privacy-aes128 privacy-password <PRIV-PASSPHRASE>
set snmp view woodshed-all oid .1 include
set snmp v3 vacm security-to-group security-model usm security-name <V3-USER> group woodshed
set snmp v3 vacm access group woodshed default-context-prefix security-model usm security-level privacy read-view woodshed-all
commit
